## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design lightweight governance frameworks for multi-team organizations with regional considerations, emphasizing practical artifacts, rituals, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- Engineering governance
- Artifacts and rituals
- Metrics and experiments

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple guardrail filter: decide if a feature request should be evaluated against guardrails
function shouldGuardrailsApply(request) {
  const highImpactPatterns = [/auth|security|data/i];
  return highImpactPatterns.some((r) => r.test(request.description));
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to translate reliability risks into concrete actions, balancing external vendor risk with internal velocity, and creating observable gates and rituals.

## Key Concepts

- Reliability budgets and SLO/SLI definitions
- Backpressure and circuit breakers in distributed systems
- Chaos testing and staged rollout plans
- Incident management and post-incident reviews

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: calculate if burn rate exceeds budget
function burnRate(slo, breaches, windowHours){
  const budget = 1 - slo;
  const spend = breaches / windowHours;
  return spend / budget;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust SLOs if the partner outage lasts longer than a day?
- What dashboards and alerts would you use to prevent reactive firefighting?
